  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass \\(m\\) is located in a one dimensional potential field where potential energy is given by : \\(\\mathrm{V}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{A}(1-\\cos \\mathrm{px})\\), where \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{p}\\) are constants. The period of small oscillations of the particle is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NC8pA",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{(A p)}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "y1Dtx",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{\\left(A p^2\\right)}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lf7XP",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{A}}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ObGAz",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2 \\pi} \\sqrt{\\frac{A p}{m}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: \\(v_x=A(1-\\cos p x)\\)\n\\(F=-\\frac{d u}{d x}=-A p \\sin p x\\)\nFor small (x)\n\\(\\mathrm{F}=-\\mathrm{AP}^2 \\mathrm{x}\\)\n\\(a=-\\frac{A p^2}{m} x \\quad a=-\\omega^2 x\\)\n\\(\\omega=\\sqrt{\\frac{A P^2}{\\mathrm{~m}}} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{T}=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{A p^2}}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
